@page "/aichat"
@using Radzen
@using Radzen.Blazor

<RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.H2" TagName="TagName.H1" class="rz-pt-8">
    Blazor AIChat
</RadzenText>
<RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Subtitle1" TagName="TagName.P" class="rz-pb-4">
    The Blazor AI Chat component provides a conversational, streaming chat interface for building AI assistants and chatbot experiences.
</RadzenText>

<RadzenExample ComponentName="AIChat" Example="AIChatConfig">
    <AIChatConfig />
</RadzenExample>

<RadzenText Anchor="aichat#custom-styling" TextStyle="TextStyle.H5" TagName="TagName.H2" class="rz-pt-12">
    Custom styling
</RadzenText>
<RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Body1" class="rz-mb-8">
    Customize the appearance of the <strong>AIChat</strong> component using <code>Style</code>, <code>ShowClearButton</code>, <code>Disabled</code>, and <code>ReadOnly</code> properties.
</RadzenText>
<RadzenExample ComponentName="AIChat" Example="AIChatCustomStyling">
    <AIChatCustomStyling />
</RadzenExample>

<RadzenText Anchor="aichat#compact-aichat" TextStyle="TextStyle.H5" TagName="TagName.H2" class="rz-pt-12">
    Compact aichat
</RadzenText>
<RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Body1" class="rz-mb-8">
    Create a more compact chat interface suitable for smaller spaces or sidebar implementations.
</RadzenText>
<RadzenExample ComponentName="AIChat" Example="AIChatCompact">
    <AIChatCompact />
</RadzenExample>

<RadzenText Anchor="aichat#events" TextStyle="TextStyle.H5" TagName="TagName.H2" class="rz-pt-12">
    Events and interactions
</RadzenText>
<RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Body1" class="rz-mb-8">
    Handle chat events like <code>MessageAdded</code>, <code>MessageSent</code>, <code>ResponseReceived</code>, and <code>ChatCleared</code> to integrate with your application logic.
</RadzenText>
<RadzenExample ComponentName="AIChat" Example="AIChatEvents">
    <AIChatEvents />
</RadzenExample>

<RadzenText Anchor="aichat#date-separator" TextStyle="TextStyle.H5" TagName="TagName.H2" class="rz-pt-12">
    Date separator and timestamp format
</RadzenText>
<RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Body1" class="rz-mb-8">
    Use <code>TimestampFormat</code> to control how the time is rendered next to each message, and <code>ShowDateSeparator</code> (with <code>DateSeparatorFormat</code>)
    to insert a divider between messages whenever the day changes — useful when restoring long conversation history via <code>LoadMessages</code>.
</RadzenText>
<RadzenExample ComponentName="AIChat" Example="AIChatDateSeparator">
    <AIChatDateSeparator />
</RadzenExample>

<RadzenText Anchor="aichat#memory" TextStyle="TextStyle.H5" TagName="TagName.H2" class="rz-pt-12">
    AI Chat with Memory
</RadzenText>
<RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Body1" class="rz-mb-8">
    The <strong>AIChat</strong> component supports conversation memory that remembers previous questions and maintains context across multiple interactions. 
    Use <code>SessionId</code> to maintain conversation state and <code>SessionIdChanged</code> to track session changes.
</RadzenText>
<RadzenExample ComponentName="AIChat" Example="AIChatWithMemory">
    <AIChatWithMemory />
</RadzenExample>

<RadzenText Anchor="aichat#tools" TextStyle="TextStyle.H5" TagName="TagName.H2" class="rz-pt-12">
    Tool calling
</RadzenText>
<RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Body1" class="rz-mb-8">
    Give the model access to your application's data and logic with the <code>Tools</code> parameter. Tools are <code>AIFunction</code> instances from
    <code>Microsoft.Extensions.AI</code> - create them from any C# method with <code>AIFunctionFactory.Create</code> and describe them with <code>[Description]</code> attributes.
    The model decides when to call a tool, <strong>AIChat</strong> invokes it, shows the call in the conversation and feeds the result back to the model.
    The <code>ToolCallCompleted</code> event fires when a tool finishes.
</RadzenText>
<RadzenExample ComponentName="AIChat" Example="AIChatTools">
    <AIChatTools />
</RadzenExample>

<RadzenText Anchor="aichat#generative-ui" TextStyle="TextStyle.H5" TagName="TagName.H2" class="rz-pt-12">
    Generative UI
</RadzenText>
<RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Body1" class="rz-mb-8">
    Use <code>ToolCallTemplate</code> to render tool results with Radzen components instead of text. The template receives a <code>ChatToolCall</code> with the tool
    <code>Name</code>, <code>Arguments</code>, <code>Status</code> and <code>Result</code>; call <code>GetResult&lt;T&gt;()</code> to deserialize the result.
    Ask for the sales by month to get a chart, or for the orders of a customer to get a data grid, directly in the conversation.
</RadzenText>
<RadzenExample ComponentName="AIChat" Example="AIChatGenerativeUI">
    <AIChatGenerativeUI />
</RadzenExample>

<RadzenText Anchor="aichat#approval" TextStyle="TextStyle.H5" TagName="TagName.H2" class="rz-pt-12">
    Human in the loop
</RadzenText>
<RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Body1" class="rz-mb-8">
    Wrap a tool in <code>ApprovalRequiredAIFunction</code> to ask the user before it runs. <strong>AIChat</strong> renders the call with its arguments and
    <strong>Approve</strong> / <strong>Reject</strong> buttons, invokes the tool only when approved and tells the model when the call was rejected.
    Use <code>ToolCallTemplate</code> with <code>ApproveToolCall</code> and <code>RejectToolCall</code> to build your own approval UI.
</RadzenText>
<RadzenExample ComponentName="AIChat" Example="AIChatApproval">
    <AIChatApproval />
</RadzenExample>

<RadzenText Anchor="aichat#voice" TextStyle="TextStyle.H5" TagName="TagName.H2" class="rz-pt-12">
    Voice input
</RadzenText>
<RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Body1" class="rz-mb-8">
    Combine <strong>AIChat</strong> with <strong>RadzenSpeechToTextButton</strong> to let users talk to the assistant: the button captures speech with the browser's speech recognition
    and its <code>Change</code> event passes the transcript to <code>SendMessage</code>.
</RadzenText>
<RadzenExample ComponentName="AIChat" Example="AIChatVoice">
    <AIChatVoice />
</RadzenExample>

<RadzenText Anchor="aichat#attachments" TextStyle="TextStyle.H5" TagName="TagName.H2" class="rz-pt-12">
    File attachments
</RadzenText>
<RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Body1" class="rz-mb-8">
    Set <code>AllowAttachments="true"</code> to let users attach files with the paperclip button, or add them from code with <code>AddAttachment</code>. Images are sent to a multimodal model as image content
    and shown in the conversation; text files such as txt, csv, md, json or xml are sent as text, so any model can answer questions about them; PDF files are sent as file content for providers that support it (OpenAI). <code>MaxAttachmentSize</code> and <code>AcceptedAttachmentTypes</code> limit what can be attached and the <code>Error</code> event reports files that
    cannot be read. <code>ShowUsage</code> displays the tokens the provider reports for each answer and the stop button next to the input cancels a response that is still streaming.
</RadzenText>
<RadzenExample ComponentName="AIChat" Example="AIChatAttachments">
    <AIChatAttachments />
</RadzenExample>

<RadzenText Anchor="aichat#providers" TextStyle="TextStyle.H5" TagName="TagName.H2" class="rz-pt-12">
    AI providers
</RadzenText>
<RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Body1" class="rz-mb-4">
    <strong>AIChat</strong> talks to the model through the <code>IChatClient</code> abstraction of <code>Microsoft.Extensions.AI</code>.
    <code>AddAIChatService</code> configures the built-in <code>OpenAICompatibleChatClient</code>, which works with any OpenAI-compatible chat completions endpoint
    (OpenAI, Azure OpenAI, Ollama, LM Studio, Cloudflare Workers AI and others) and supports streaming and tool calling.
</RadzenText>
<pre>
<code>
builder.Services.AddAIChatService(options =>
{
    options.Endpoint = "https://api.openai.com/v1/chat/completions";
    options.ApiKey = builder.Configuration["OpenAI:ApiKey"];
    options.Model = "gpt-4o-mini";
    options.EmbeddingsModel = "text-embedding-3-small";
});
</code>
</pre>
<RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Body1" class="rz-mb-4">
    To use a different provider, register its <code>IChatClient</code> and <strong>AIChat</strong> picks it up automatically. Any middleware added with
    <code>ChatClientBuilder</code> (logging, caching, OpenTelemetry, rate limiting) applies to the chat as well.
</RadzenText>
<pre>
<code>
// OpenAI (Microsoft.Extensions.AI.OpenAI)
builder.Services.AddChatClient(new OpenAIClient(apiKey).GetChatClient("gpt-4o-mini").AsIChatClient())
    .UseLogging();

// Azure OpenAI (Azure.AI.OpenAI + Microsoft.Extensions.AI.OpenAI)
builder.Services.AddChatClient(new AzureOpenAIClient(new Uri(endpoint), new DefaultAzureCredential()).GetChatClient("gpt-4o-mini").AsIChatClient());

// Ollama (OllamaSharp)
builder.Services.AddChatClient(new OllamaApiClient(new Uri("http://localhost:11434"), "llama3.2"));

builder.Services.AddAIChatService();
</code>
</pre>

<RadzenText Anchor="aichat#configuration" TextStyle="TextStyle.H5" TagName="TagName.H2" class="rz-pt-12">
    Runtime AI Configuration
</RadzenText>
<RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Body1" class="rz-mb-8">
    Customize AI behavior at runtime by configuring the <code>Model</code>, <code>Temperature</code>, <code>MaxTokens</code>, <code>SystemPrompt</code>, <code>Endpoint</code>, <code>Proxy</code>, <code>ApiKey</code>, and <code>ApiKeyHeader</code> parameters. 
    These parameters can be set on the component or passed to the <code>SendMessage</code> method to override settings per message, enabling dynamic switching between different AI providers and models.
</RadzenText>
<RadzenExample ComponentName="AIChat" Example="AIChatModelSelection">
    <AIChatModelSelection />
</RadzenExample> 